# Secrets — API keys and Google OAuth material; never commit any of these
.env
client_secret*.json
.gmail_token.json

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# Audit dumps and scheduled-run logs are local run artifacts, keep them out of
# the repo. The .log line matters: the runbook's cron line redirects into
# audit/cron.log, which is not a .json and would otherwise be committed. The .csv line
# matters just as much: deals_v4_migrate.py's human-reviewable audit (deal names,
# lead_source) is real business data and must never land in git history.
audit/*.json
audit/*.log
audit/*.csv

# Dashboard build output. Regenerated from live HubSpot on every run, so a committed copy is
# only ever a stale snapshot that looks authoritative in a diff. CI builds it fresh and uploads
# it straight to the Pages artifact — it never needs to be in the repo.
dashboard/ops_dashboard_data.json